{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity","id":1405590,"title":"V5 and a discussion regarding Humanity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-31T09:09:19-07:00","id":1405590,"title":"V5 and a discussion regarding Humanity","content":"Ok, I recently began a V5 chronicle and would like to get an opinion from the rest of you.<br /> <br /> So, my chronicle has the following tenets:<ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We Are Not Beasts - Do not kill or maim for pleasure. Control your Hunger. Do not give in to needless cruelty towards the kine.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Companionship - Respect your coterie. They are your brothers and sisters of the night, and you only have each other.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thou shalt not harm the innocent - Purity is a commodity that is rare in this world. Tarnishing the purity of childhood (killing or harming children, for example) makes the world a darker place.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> In our previous session, the coterie was attacked by another coterie. At one point, the group had incapacitated one of their opponents, who had dropped into torpor. The Malkavian in the group was the one that made the incapacitating shot, which he scored a messy critical on. He decided that his messy critical would be to unload the clip of his gun into the face of the torporous vampire, which dusted him.<br /> <br /> A few moments later, the group incapacitated a second vampire, knocking him into torpor. The same character rolled a bestial failure on a roll, and he decided that he would drain the torporous vampire. No, he didn't commit diablerie, but he killed the vampire by draining him completely.<br /> <br /> Considering the chronicle tenets, I ruled that the Malkavian violated the tenet &quot;We Are Not Beasts&quot; by cruelly killing two incapacitated enemies and thus incurred a stain on his humanity (keep in mind that he has a Humanity of 8). He is arguing that it does not violate the tenets.<br /> <br /> I'd like to hear opinions.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","name":"Raunalyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T09:43:06-07:00","id":1405593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raunalyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity#post1405590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I recently began a V5 chronicle and would like to get an opinion from the rest of you.<br /> <br /> So, my chronicle has the following tenets:<ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We Are Not Beasts - Do not kill or maim for pleasure. Control your Hunger. Do not give in to needless cruelty towards the kine.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kill or maim <b>for pleasure</b>? Nope.<br /> Control your<b> Hunger</b>? Maybe violated this one, would need more info to make proper assessment. Do convictions negate this, what was his hunger level, etc.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Give in to needless cruelty towards the <b>kine</b>? Nope, vampires are not kine.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raunalyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity#post1405590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ruled that the Malkavian violated the tenet &quot;We Are Not Beasts&quot; by cruelly killing two incapacitated enemies and thus incurred a stain on his humanity (keep in mind that he has a Humanity of 8). He is arguing that it does not violate the tenets.<br /> <br /> I'd like to hear opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> He may have gained one based on how your convictions are written but not because he cruelly killed vampires, nothing in your tenets prevents this action.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T09:47:53-07:00","id":1405595,"title":"","content":"No. Killing them was neither cruel nor needless. Just efficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T11:21:49-07:00","id":1405629,"title":"","content":"Question. The way you describe it makes it sound like the first kill happened during combat rather than after. Did the &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">incapacitating shot&quot; end up killing their opponent rather than shooting them dead after they were already down, is that correct?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T12:53:45-07:00","id":1405656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405629#post1405629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question. The way you describe it makes it sound like the first kill happened during combat rather than after. Did the &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">incapacitating shot&quot; end up killing their opponent rather than shooting them dead after they were already down, is that correct?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The Malkavian's first shot incapacitated the target. He then emptied his entire clip into the face of the incapacitated target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","name":"Raunalyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T14:04:34-07:00","id":1405665,"title":"","content":"I think your ruling is fine because the player choose to kill the second vampire. You let him choose how the second bestial failure should have happened and his choice was to kill a second time in the span of a few minutes or less and that violates the tenet &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do not kill or maim for pleasure&quot;.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T14:40:38-07:00","id":1405667,"title":"","content":"But was it for pleasure or simply because killing the second vampire was the most efficient way to ensure that the defeated vampire didn\u2019t bother him again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T16:52:08-07:00","id":1405695,"title":"","content":"What is a Humanity 8 character doing getting into vampire gang fights and emptying clips into downed opponents, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T20:59:04-07:00","id":1405735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raunalyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405656#post1405656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Malkavian's first shot incapacitated the target. He then emptied his entire clip into the face of the incapacitated target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, got it.<br /> <br /> Also, I second Matt's question above. Why is a Humanity 8 character literally shooting helpless opponents in the face? Your call sounds reasonable. Perhaps, though, you could give us a quick summary of why your player thinks differently? As in, what's his argument? Unless you feel that would be indulging him too much on this and create further problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T02:23:02-07:00","id":1405765,"title":"","content":"Okay. I guess if you consider killing a helpless opponent a sin against Humanity then I agree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T02:27:33-07:00","id":1405766,"title":"","content":"I mean, it\u2019s not like it\u2019s a baby or a child or anything. It\u2019s an armed enemy who was tryna kill you. And who now hates you twice as much as before. My characters rarely get involved in combat unless they have to, and when they do they would certainly accept an honorable surrender, but if another vampire\u2019s trying to destroy you and you knock them out it only makes sense to decapitate them before they can get up again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T08:02:12-07:00","id":1405791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405766#post1405766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it\u2019s not like it\u2019s a baby or a child or anything. It\u2019s an armed enemy who was tryna kill you. And who now hates you twice as much as before. My characters rarely get involved in combat unless they have to, and when they do they would certainly accept an honorable surrender, but if another vampire\u2019s trying to destroy you and you knock them out it only makes sense to decapitate them before they can get up again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are those characters if yours Humanity 8 vampires, though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T10:31:37-07:00","id":1405805,"title":"","content":"No, but...<br /> <br /> Ohhhh. I see what you mean. I guess killing a helpless opponent is kinda cold-blooded from a Humanity perspective.<br /> <br /> But still. There\u2019s nothing in the OP\u2019s Tenets that prohibits it. There is a clause against \u201ccruelty\u201d but is it cruel to kill a helpless opponent? (Not being snarky here. 100% serious.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T10:32:53-07:00","id":1405806,"title":"","content":"And it\u2019s not for pleasure either. It\u2019s for business reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T10:38:33-07:00","id":1405807,"title":"","content":"When characters lose contol due to something they couldn't possibly forsee, It's wise to be leniant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T10:45:50-07:00","id":1405810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405807#post1405807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When characters lose contol due to something they couldn't possibly forsee, It's wise to be leniant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to be a running theme with messy criticals and the Hunger system. Not overly fond of that myself. It feels patronising. But yes, you have a point. Perhaps those rolls could've resulted in something less, well, kill-y?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T10:52:55-07:00","id":1405812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405807#post1405807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When characters lose contol due to something they couldn't possibly forsee, It's wise to be leniant.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is true in the case made by the OP the player was given freedom to decide how the messy critical should have gone and he chose to kill the helpless opponent right after he had done the same a few moments before. He could have chosen to break the opposing vampire's legs or something similar, painful but not lethal, he could have used some form of dominate or something else, insted he went for the kill twice in a row and it was not the ST forcing the player to kill but the player deciding it was appropriate to do so.<br /> <br /> The ST's call is perfectly fine imo.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T12:12:05-07:00","id":1405819,"title":"","content":"I think that the player's right. Unless &quot;do not kill or maim for pleasure&quot; means &quot;do not kill&quot; (at all) and &quot;do not maim for pleasure&quot;, there's nothing that prohibits killing kindred under any circumstances. You probably meant that when you came up with the tenets, but you don't have it in writing. An example of a tenet in the core samples that could penalise that behaviour is &quot;Thou shalt not kill, save in self defense&quot;.<br /> <br /> Technically, as the results of a messy critical and a bestial failure, they could come under &quot;control your hunger&quot;, but then so would getting any compulsion, regardless of what they do in that state of mind. By itself, the letter of that sentence could be very strict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T16:22:48-07:00","id":1405851,"title":"","content":"If I were a playing a character with a humanity of 8, and the Beast got the better of my character and I lost my shit, killing torpored foes, I'd be okay with that stain. I think its fair for the ST to say that constitutes a stain under the first chronicle tenet. This isn't the supreme court, with people lawyering the &quot;plain meaning of the tenet&quot;, contextualism, constructivist and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T19:45:44-07:00","id":1405866,"title":"","content":"Basically Humanity just means being a good person. Tenets just highlight different facets of that philosophy. Would a good person kill a torpored foe? I think the answer is yes so I would say it\u2019s not a stain. Someone else might say the opposite. It\u2019s a judgment call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T22:59:09-07:00","id":1405885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405812#post1405812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While this is true in the case made by the OP the player was given freedom to decide how the messy critical should have gone and he chose to kill the helpless opponent right after he had done the same a few moments before. He could have chosen to break the opposing vampire's legs or something similar, painful but not lethal, he could have used some form of dominate or something else, insted he went for the kill twice in a row and it was not the ST forcing the player to kill but the player deciding it was appropriate to do so.<br /> <br /> The ST's call is perfectly fine imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is <i>wrong</i> <br /> If you encourage your players to rollplay their beasts lightly and harmlessly, they won't rollplay the beasts at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T03:23:55-07:00","id":1405907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405885#post1405885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is <i>wrong</i><br /> If you encourage your players to rollplay their beasts lightly and harmlessly, they won't rollplay the beasts at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>This opinion of yours is predictably in line with your usual philosophy:&quot;Let players do whatever suits their fancy and don't you dare enforcing consequences for their actions&quot;.<br /> <br /> Players are <b>free to make their own choices</b> but they should also be aware those choices have <b>consequences</b> attached to them.<br /> <br /> If a player wants to be a murderhobo, killing and diablerizing right and left and generally being antisocial and power hungry, screwing others in the course of play he's <b>making a choice and that should be respected.</b><br /> <br /> <b>That does not mean those actions don't have consequences and the ST should absolutely enforce them</b>.<br /> <br /> In this case the player was given agency on how to portray his Character's actions. He choose to kill twice in the span of minutes when he could have done something different. We don't know if the player was trying to ROLEplay his character or just wanted to act antisocially for the shake of it. That doesn't really matter though. What matters is he had a choice and he choose killing when he had other options potentially as or more poignant and that action warrants a stain on humanity (as many other people noted, especially because the PC is supposed to be a humanity 8 vamp, which means he should be more huiman than most humans alive).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T04:28:45-07:00","id":1405913,"title":"","content":"We're talking about a the beast taking control of their characters. The players were rollplaying choices they <i>didn't</i> want to make. &quot;Oh your character lost control to the monster inside of her and as a player you thought it fitting that the monster chose to do this heinous thing rather than a less heinous thing you totally could've done- Shame on you&quot; doesn't fly for reasonable people. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405907#post1405907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This opinion of yours is predictably in line with your usual philosophy:&quot;Let players do whatever suits their fancy and don't you dare enforcing consequences for their actions&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only conclude you came to this assumption by seeing that i've flatly disagreed with you now and before and now want to imagine me as a silly caricature so that you can reassure yourself that I am wrong and wrong and dumb and you are right, righteous and smart. Let me comfort you: My games are filled with 5th gen humanity 9 Baali murderhobos and I've never killed off a single one of my PCs (or the foolish players who played them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T06:20:17-07:00","id":1405924,"title":"","content":"I mean, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a> is right, Humanity 8 is more human than most people, so I guess I can see giving him a stain for that. But at the same time, I still don\u2019t think killing an unconscious enemy is inherently a stain on Humanity. It\u2019s not cruel and it\u2019s not needless, so in my opinion it doesn\u2019t violate the OP\u2019s tenets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T06:35:59-07:00","id":1405927,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a> I thought about your argument for a few minutes and I\u2019ve reconsidered. I think I was thinking more from emotion than from reason originally. The player was Humanity 8 (more human than most people), it was a pretty gruesome killing, he had other options available and he basically killed two helpless Kindred in the span of a few minutes. Under the circumstances, giving him a stain was totally within the ST\u2019s discretion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T06:47:42-07:00","id":1405933,"title":"","content":"I think there are situations where relatively high humanity individuals would kill enemies at their mercy, they would totally do this. But it would still risk humanity. They might get lucky and their conviction holds even through self reflection, or it might turn out to take its toll on their soul and maybe they become colder in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T06:57:05-07:00","id":1405939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405933#post1405933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there are situations where relatively high humanity individuals would kill enemies at their mercy, they would totally do this. But it would still risk humanity. They might get lucky and their conviction holds even through self reflection, or it might turn out to take its toll on their soul and maybe they become colder in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. That makes a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T08:16:04-07:00","id":1405945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405927#post1405927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a> I thought about your argument for a few minutes and I\u2019ve reconsidered. I think I was thinking more from emotion than from reason originally. The player was Humanity 8 (more human than most people), it was a pretty gruesome killing, he had other options available and he basically killed two helpless Kindred in the span of a few minutes. Under the circumstances, giving him a stain was totally within the ST\u2019s discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to note that a single stain for a couple of killings in a row is a pretty mild consequence. A stain is not garanteed to result in humanity loss after all. A PC could feel remorse for his own actions and thus mantain humanity. Personally I feel like a humanity 8 vampire would question his own morality after a double murder even if the people he killed were enemies. They were incapacitated and did not pose an active menace anymore, bestial failure means the PC loses control but the ST gave the player the choice to determine the outcome of the roll. The player chose to kill twice.<br /> <br /> It seems pretty clear to me even if he was not in complete control of himself the high humanity PC should absolutely question his own morality the moment he realizes what he did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T08:45:40-07:00","id":1405951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405913#post1405913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about a the beast taking control of their characters. The players were rollplaying choices they <i>didn't</i> want to make. &quot;Oh your character lost control to the monster inside of her and as a player you thought it fitting that the monster chose to do this heinous thing rather than a less heinous thing you totally could've done- Shame on you&quot; doesn't fly for reasonable people.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact the beast was in control means nothing. The actions the player chose to enact determined the POTENTIAL loss of humanity (a stain does not cause an automatic loss but rather the chance of losing humanity if you cannot find within yourself to repent for what you have done) because he choose to kill two people in cold blood when he had an alternative.<br /> <br /> He could have ROLEplayed something like this:&quot;<i>When all is said and done the lick is lays sprawled on the ground, a stake made of ash wood protruding from his chest just above his dead heart. I walk towards him, slowly but with a determination born of the rage boiling in my guts. I seem collected but the Beast is screaming to me to punish the upstart who just threatened me and my friends. As I reach him I very deliberately stare at his immobile form and then raise my foot in the air before bringing it down at full force on his right knee. A loud, satisfying CRACK, rings in the air as bones shatter. He does not make a noise but inside me I know he felt that. Despite all of my pretended morality my soul rejoices at the thought of punishing the wicked. I intended to do this just once and then stop but something snaps inside me and suddenly I find myself hitting the prone vampire again, again and again. By the time my companions manage to restrain me his legs have been shattered in multiple points, his undead flesh reduced to a bloody pulp. It will take him some time and much blood to heal them correctly. Strangely, I don't feel regret for what I just did. He was trying to kill us and he deserved to be punished, yet I realize the Beast taking control like that is worrisome... what if I lose control again and there's no one near capable of stopping me in time? I need to be more careful or one of these nights I might end up doing something I will truly regret, losing a part of myself in the process</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> Given the Chronicle tenets this would have been acceptable and not nearly as damning as killing two incapacitated enemies in the span of a few minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 08-02-2020, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T09:24:10-07:00","id":1405955,"title":"","content":"So you want players to cheese things with unintentionally funny monologues? There are only so many hours in the game. <br /> <br /> <br /> Did the characters kill people? yes. They get stains for that. <br /> Did the characters break chronicle tennets? No. They were victims of an unavoidable beast seizure. They could have reasonably done very little to mitigate that. The beast took control, it wasn't your fault, it did a thing that was slightly worse than what you were already doing. No stains. Quite frankly it doesn't matter if you shoot the guy in the head a couple of times or if you use a gun that goes Brrrrrrrr; your intent was the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T10:18:02-07:00","id":1405959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405955#post1405955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you want players to cheese things with unintentionally funny monologues? There are only so many hours in the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Did the characters kill people? yes. They get stains for that.</b><br /> Did the characters break chronicle tennets? No. They were victims of an unavoidable beast seizure. <b>They could have reasonably done very little to mitigate that</b>. The beast took control, it wasn't your fault, it did a thing that was slightly worse than what you were already doing. No stains. Quite frankly it doesn't matter if you shoot the guy in the head a couple of times or if you use a gun that goes Brrrrrrrr; your intent was the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they could have done a lot to mitigate that, for example not killing the incapacitated opponents. Unfortunately this simple fact seems to elude your comprehension though.<br /> <br /> Edit: corrected an assumption","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 08-02-2020, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T10:45:54-07:00","id":1405962,"title":"","content":"It wasn't them, it was the Beast. &quot;Unfortunately this simple fact seems to elude your comprehension though&quot; <br /> <br /> And in V5, the only way to mitigate the beast is to drain a motherfucker to death each night. Having a hunger die or two is the humane way to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T10:58:19-07:00","id":1405963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405951#post1405951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact the beast was in control means nothing. The actions the player chose to enact determined the POTENTIAL loss of humanity (a stain does not cause an automatic loss but rather the chance of losing humanity if you cannot find within yourself to repent for what you have done) because he choose to kill two people in cold blood when he had an alternative.<br /> <br /> He could have ROLEplayed something like this:&amp;quot;<i>When all is said and done the lick is lays sprawled on the ground, a stake made of ash wood protruding from his chest just above his dead heart. I walk towards him, slowly but with a determination born of the rage boiling in my guts. I seem collected but the Beast is screaming to me to punish the upstart who just threatened me and my friends. As I reach him I very deliberately stare at his immobile form and then raise my foot in the air before bringing it down at full force on his right knee. A loud, satisfying CRACK, rings in the air as bones shatter. He does not make a noise but inside me I know he felt that. Despite all of my pretended morality my soul rejoices at the thought of punishing the wicked. I intended to do this just once and then stop but something snaps inside me and suddenly I find myself hitting the prone vampire again, again and again. By the time my companions manage to restrain me his legs have been shattered in multiple points, his undead flesh reduced to a bloody pulp. It will take him some time and much blood to heal them correctly. Strangely, I don't feel regret for what I just did. He was trying to kill us and he deserved to be punished, yet I realize the Beast taking control like that is worrisome... what if I lose control again and there's no one near capable of stopping me in time? I need to be more careful or one of these nights I might end up doing something I will truly regret, losing a part of myself in the process</i>&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Given the Chronicle tenets this would have been acceptable and not nearly as damning as killing two incapacitated enemies in the span of a few minutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool monologue. Really shows the character\u2019s inner conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T11:00:31-07:00","id":1405965,"title":"","content":"Actually, this discussion is getting a little heated. Imma bow out now and go read Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T11:18:58-07:00","id":1405971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405962#post1405962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't them, it was the Beast. &quot;Unfortunately this simple fact seems to elude your comprehension though&quot;<br /> <br /> And in V5, the only way to mitigate the beast is to drain a motherfucker to death each night. Having a hunger die or two is the humane way to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was them all right, because the ST gave them agency and they chose to resolve the messy criticals by killing incapacitated opponents twice in a row.<br /> <br /> A messy Critical does not mean you automatically kill people. The player chose to kill and that action deserves a stain, especially considering how the killer was a humanity 8 vampire.<br /> <br /> And the fact that in V5 you can completely sate your hunger only by killing has no bearing with the fact that killing two incapacitated opponents as an high humanity Vampire deserves a stain (Or more depending on the chronicle tenets).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 08-02-2020, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T11:45:22-07:00","id":1405973,"title":"","content":"A stain is not an automatic loss of a humanity. To me, either way, it's a role playing opportunity. I succeed on the roll: &quot;Man, I can't believe I did that...I didn't have to do that. What the fuck am doing?&quot; I fail the roll? &quot;Fucker had it coming..&quot; Either way, the character's story progresses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T13:34:41-07:00","id":1405987,"title":"","content":"The st gave the players agency to faithfully play the character's lack of agency. <br /> <br /> I know, I know; a lot of people aren't good at distinguishing between the two. But we really, really shouldn't reasonably want players to control their beasts as if they were just the normal characters but a bit more emotional. That's not what the beast is. you're acting like the players did bad because they didn't use their control over the beast to put the gun down, run to the nearest church and pray the day away. a character is not his beast even if the player has agency over both (unless we're discussing Instict paths but this is a v5 thread)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T15:08:44-07:00","id":1406005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405987#post1405987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The st gave the players agency to faithfully play the character's lack of agency.<br /> <br /> I know, I know; a lot of people aren't good at distinguishing between the two. But we really, really shouldn't reasonably want players to control their beasts as if they were just the normal characters but a bit more emotional. That's not what the beast is. you're acting like the players did bad because they didn't use their control over the beast to put the gun down, run to the nearest church and pray the day away. a character is not his beast even if the player has agency over both (unless we're discussing Instict paths but this is a v5 thread)</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between automatic loss and your character recoiling in horror for what they did. Loss of humanity always represents in every edition justifying what you just did. THis is the EQUIVALENT of a V20 and early edition humanity Roll. That's what a stain is. And its EVEN LESS than that at Humanity eight he needs to get 8 stains in 1 night without doing ANYTHING to show removes to degenerate... and even then the player can choose to not lose the humanity and try and remorse their way back.<br /> <br /> But yeah getting stains because your character lost them self to the beast or even have to roll humanity checks is a suggested way of dealing with it. If you're letting people not count frenzy for their actions you're definately not playing RAI or RAW....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T15:21:54-07:00","id":1406008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1405987#post1405987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The st gave the players agency to faithfully play the character's lack of agency.<br /> <br /> I know, I know; a lot of people aren't good at distinguishing between the two. But we really, really shouldn't reasonably want players to control their beasts as if they were just the normal characters but a bit more emotional. That's not what the beast is. you're acting like the players did bad because they didn't use their control over the beast to put the gun down, run to the nearest church and pray the day away. a character is not his beast even if the player has agency over both (unless we're discussing Instict paths but this is a v5 thread)</div> </div> </div> </div>You are not even trying to make sense anymore.<br /> <br /> A messy critical is an event that involves you suceeding BUT at the same time the beast rears its ugly head and causes you to act more violently than intended. You disarm your fencing opponent but instead of just taking away his blade you shatter his wrist, or you manage to hack into the mainframe but in doing so you break the device you were using and so on. Nowhere it's mentioned your loss of control means you have to kill.<br /> <br /> In this specific case the player was told to choose the outcome of the roll and he decided for a double murder. It's a respectable choice from a ROLEplaying point of view but then I can't see how the player could claim he doesn't deserve a stain (which under V5 rules is very mild as an outcome). He could have chosen something less drastic and avoided the stain. He had other options and chose to kill, and in VtM killing in cold blood as a humanity 8 character has consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T16:52:28-07:00","id":1406015,"title":"","content":"I get the impression that the player in question doesn't have a good understanding of what the Humanity system represents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 08-02-2020, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T18:56:19-07:00","id":1406034,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see your primary mistake. <br /> <br /> The players killed their opponents with bestial successes on a -would be- incapacitating shot. They aren't knocking vampires out nicely and executing them, one of them is at least shooting his foe till he goea down, and the beast got him carried away at the end. <br /> <br /> now, in most people's books, riddling someone with bullets is not a safe way to incapacitate someone. The character must have used his weapon with good understanding that his opponent could reach final death from 'overkill' even if we don't take into account the beast. In most countries this wouldn't even get a 'third degree murder/x degree manslaughter to it. The player should certainly get stains for murder and move on. <br /> <br /> For the -drain after downing- player... well, that's a more grey area. IDK if that rulling of what happened is even correct; Draining an incapacitated vampire should lead to torpor, not final death, and i think that's a legitimate way of dealing with a kindred foe without murdering them. But as it is murder here, you may potentially have a point in thia case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T08:50:17-07:00","id":1406117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405590-v5-and-a-discussion-regarding-humanity?p=1406034#post1406034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see your primary mistake.<br /> <br /> The players killed their opponents with bestial successes on a -would be- incapacitating shot. They aren't knocking vampires out nicely and executing them, one of them is at least shooting his foe till he goea down, and the beast got him carried away at the end.<br /> <br /> now, in most people's books, riddling someone with bullets is not a safe way to incapacitate someone. The character must have used his weapon with good understanding that his opponent could reach final death from 'overkill' even if we don't take into account the beast. In most countries this wouldn't even get a 'third degree murder/x degree manslaughter to it. The player should certainly get stains for murder and move on.<br /> <br /> For the -drain after downing- player... well, that's a more grey area. IDK if that rulling of what happened is even correct; Draining an incapacitated vampire should lead to torpor, not final death, and i think that's a legitimate way of dealing with a kindred foe without murdering them. But as it is murder here, you may potentially have a point in thia case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Being OK with the Beast's actions is represented in ALL versions of vampire with degeneration. AT no point are you intended to be able to go &quot;The Beast made me do it so its ok&quot; but rather be horrified by it. Saying they should avoid degeneration because the Beast takes over would be like if you frenzy and run through a fire complaining they shouldn't have any damage because &quot;they lacked control&quot;<br /> <br /> But the character litterally has options here. They spend time freaking our... or they don't and move on and degenerate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}